in/smoke/`), gate scenario 2 → adapter + loss curve saved.\n\n## Acceptance (BDD)\n```gherkin\nFeature: the QLoRA trainer is proven on real RDNA4 eGPU hardware\n  Scenario: the eGPU enumerates for compute\n    Given the Razer Core X + RX 9060 XT attached to the T480 over Thunderbolt-3\n    And ROCm-on-Windows (or the WSL2 fallback) installed\n    When the gate probes the compute device\n    Then rocm-smi / hipInfo reports gfx1200 with ~16GB VRAM\n\n  Scenario: a real QLoRA step completes and saves\n    Given Unsloth installed on the enumerated device\n    When a ~30-step 4-bit QLoRA runs on Qwen2.5-Coder-7B over a toy dataset\n    Then training loss is recorded for every step and decreases overall\n    And a LoRA adapter is written to disk and reloads without error\n\n  Scenario: honest failure when the GPU is unavailable\n    Given no compute device reports gfx1200\n    When the gate runs\n    Then it exits non-zero with reason gpu_absent and marks nothing as passed\n```\n\n## Out of scope\nThe real training corpus (T2/T3), the home clone (T1), any serving wiring (T4). Toy data only here.\n\n## Handoff\nVerifier re-runs `scripts/gates/t0.py` on the T480 with the eGPU attached; gate output records the\nROCm build, device string, VRAM, step count, and final loss. `docs/train/T0-trainer-evidence.md`\ncaptures `rocm-smi` output + the loss curve + which path worked (native-Windows vs WSL2) — this\nresolves the plan's open OS decision.\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"98b3b77b-b0cc-4923-bdf8-ac725673fa76","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"61a9f7a2-1353-4f19-addd-895289cb8f19","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
