{"parentUuid":"d747d369-59aa-4243-894b-68e0a52a230d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1af580f8-ee8a-4843-8603-75148e8a4d83","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0134tKLKZ8gYkHyXH6fQvLUn","type":"tool_result","content":"# Unsloth Studio Windows Installer Analysis\n\n## Core Purpose\nThis PowerShell script installs Unsloth Studio, a machine learning framework, on Windows systems with automatic dependency resolution and GPU detection.\n\n## Step-by-Step Process\n\n### 1. **Dependency Detection & Installation**\nThe script checks for and installs:\n- **Python 3.11-3.13**: Searches system PATH; if missing, uses `winget install Python.Python.$PythonVersion` or falls back to downloading from `https://www.python.org/ftp/python/`\n- **uv package manager** (v0.8.16+): Via `winget install astral-sh.uv` or `https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1`\n- **Virtual environment**: Created using `uv venv $VenvDir --python \"$PythonPath\"`\n\n### 2. **GPU Architecture Detection**\n\n**NVIDIA**: Searches for `nvidia-smi.exe` via PATH and hardcoded locations (`$env:ProgramFiles\\NVIDIA Corporation\\NVSMI\\`), then runs `nvidia-smi -L` to confirm GPU presence.\n\n**AMD ROCm**: Multi-stage detection:\n- Locates `hipinfo.exe` via PATH or `$env:HIP_PATH`/`$env:ROCM_PATH`\n- Executes `hipinfo` to extract \"gcnArchName\" (GPU architecture like `gfx1151`, `gfx1200`)\n- Falls back to `amd-smi list` (with `__COMPAT_LAYER=RunAsInvoker` to suppress UAC prompts)\n- Uses WMI `Get-WmiObject Win32_VideoController` to infer arch from GPU marketing names (e.g., \"RX 7900\" → `gfx1100`)\n- Queries `hipconfig --version` or `amd-smi version` for ROCm version string\n\nEnvironment variables override detection: `$env:UNSLOTH_ROCM_GFX_ARCH` pins the architecture.\n\n### 3. **Installation Directories**\n\nThe script resolves install location via priority order:\n- `$env:UNSLOTH_STUDIO_HOME` (if set)\n- `$env:STUDIO_HOME` (alias)\n- `$env:USERPROFILE\\.unsloth\\studio` (default)\n\nCreates subdirectories:\n- `unsloth_studio/` – Python venv\n- `share/` – configuration and data\n- LOCALAPPDATA\\Unsloth Studio (Windows Standard)\n\n### 4. **Core Installation Commands**\n\n```\nuv venv $VenvDir --python \"$ResolvedPythonExePath\"\n```\n\nThe script then installs the `unsloth` package (customizable via `--package` flag) into this venv. PyTorch installation can be skipped with `--no-torch` or `$env:UNSLOTH_NO_TORCH=1`.\n\n### 5. **Shortcut Creation**\n\nGenerates `launch-studio.ps1` launcher script that:\n- Tests if Unsloth is healthy via `http://127.0.0.1:$port/api/health`\n- Spawns the backend on a free port (8888–8908)\n- Opens the browser to localhost\n- Creates Windows shortcuts (Desktop + Start Menu) pointing to PowerShell with this launcher\n\nIcon fetched from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unslothai/unsloth/main/studio/frontend/public/unsloth.ico`\n\n### 6. **PyTorch/Torch Index**\n\nThe script sets environment variables to control wheel installation source:\n```\nUV_NO_CONFIG=1\nUV_HTTP_RETRIES=5\nUV_HTTP_TIMEOUT=180\nUV_COMPILE_BYTECODE_TIMEOUT=180\n```\n\nWhen installing torch, it clears competing index env vars (`UV_DEFAULT_INDEX`, `UV_INDEX_URL`) and uses `--default-index` to pin a specific PyTorch repository. No explicit ROCm or bitsandbytes version is hard-coded in this script; those are delegated to the uv resolver.\n\n### 7. **Privilege & Security**\n\n- **No admin required**: Per-user Python install via `InstallAllUsers=0`; User PATH registry update via `HKCU\\Environment\\Path`\n- **Icon cache refresh**: Calls `ie4uinit.exe -ClearIconCache` and kills `StartMenuExperienceHost` to refresh tiles\n- **Credential redaction**: Strips userinfo, query params, and fragments from index URLs before printing installer errors\n- **Rollback on failure**: Preserves prior venv with timestamp suffix; restores on install error\n\n### 8. **Network Endpoints Contacted**\n\n- `https://www.python.org/ftp/python/` – version listing and installer download\n- `https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1` – uv fallback installer\n- `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unslothai/unsloth/main/studio/frontend/public/unsloth.ico` – application icon\n- PyTorch index URL (custom, specified by installer or `$env:UNSLOTH_TORCH_INDEX_URL`)\n\n### 9. **Conda Rejection**\n\nThe script explicitly skips Anaconda/Miniconda interpreters by checking executable path and `sys.base_prefix` against pattern `(?i)(conda|miniconda|anaconda|miniforge|mambaforge)`. This avoids DLL path issues that break PyTorch on Windows.\n\n### 10. **Optional Features**\n\n- `--local`: Develops from repo (requires `pyproject.toml`)\n- `--tauri`: Desktop app mode (restricts custom install paths)\n- `--shortcuts-only`: Regenerate launchers without reinstalling\n- `--with-llama-cpp-dir`: Integrate llama.cpp build\n- `--verbose` / `-v`: Stream full command output (redacts credentials)"}]},"uuid":"d93d2d38-6071-41b1-aa7e-443fc32ace6f","timestamp":"2026-07-22T16:51:09.068Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":154358,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Unsloth Studio Windows Installer Analysis\n\n## Core Purpose\nThis PowerShell script installs Unsloth Studio, a machine learning framework, on Windows systems with automatic dependency resolution and GPU detection.\n\n## Step-by-Step Process\n\n### 1. **Dependency Detection & Installation**\nThe script checks for and installs:\n- **Python 3.11-3.13**: Searches system PATH; if missing, uses `winget install Python.Python.$PythonVersion` or falls back to downloading from `https://www.python.org/ftp/python/`\n- **uv package manager** (v0.8.16+): Via `winget install astral-sh.uv` or `https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1`\n- **Virtual environment**: Created using `uv venv $VenvDir --python \"$PythonPath\"`\n\n### 2. **GPU Architecture Detection**\n\n**NVIDIA**: Searches for `nvidia-smi.exe` via PATH and hardcoded locations (`$env:ProgramFiles\\NVIDIA Corporation\\NVSMI\\`), then runs `nvidia-smi -L` to confirm GPU presence.\n\n**AMD ROCm**: Mu