{"parentUuid":"ba0c0a39-ffa3-458c-80f7-ea08b28d42ef","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"85b8b153-3abc-4db9-9e9e-9fcc277f5e21","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111n8zXU7mLHf2Gfj7NnEwj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Prime-Silo Home — the single declared home\n2\t\n3\tPrime-Silo keeps all of its workspace data under **one declared home\n4\tdirectory**, with everything else derived from it:\n5\t\n6\t```\n7\t<home>/                       ← the declared Prime-Silo home\n8\t├── customware/               ← Space server data (L1/L2 modules)   → CUSTOMWARE_PATH\n9\t└── benny/                    ← portable Benny runtime              → $BENNY_HOME\n10\t    ├── bin/  config/  data/  workspaces/  models/  logs/  state/  …\n11\t```\n12\t\n13\tOne resolver decides where the home is, and every process — the desktop\n14\tshell, the tray, the Space server, `node space serve/supervise`, and the\n15\tPython runtime — asks the same resolver:\n16\t\n17\t- Node: `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js` (`resolveHome()`)\n18\t- Python: `benny.portable.home.resolve_home()` / `resolve_benny_home()`\n19\t\n20\t## Resolution precedence (highest wins)\n21\t\n22\t| #   | Source                                                                 | Provenance tag |\n23\t| --- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n24\t| 1   | `PRIME_SILO_HOME` environment variable                                 | `env`          |\n25\t| 2   | `homeDir` in `prime-silo-config.json` (set via tray \"Configure Home…\") | `config`       |\n26\t| 3   | Per-user default: `<appData>/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-home`               | `default`      |\n27\t\n28\tDerived paths can still be overridden individually — an explicit\n29\t`BENNY_HOME` or `CUSTOMWARE_PATH` env var always wins for its own path —\n30\tbut the override is _reported_, not silent: it carries an `env-override`\n31\tsource tag and a divergence warning when it points outside the declared\n32\thome.\n33\t\n34\t**There is no repo-relative fallback.** Nothing writes into a git checkout\n35\twhen the home is unconfigured; the per-user default is used instead.\n36\t\n37\t## Checking where your home is (and why)\n38\t\n39\t- **Tray** — right-click the Prime-Silo tray icon: one `Home: <name> (source)`\n40\t  entry whose submenu holds everything home-related — **Open workspaces\n41\t  (runs & outputs)** first (that's where generated deliverables land, e.g.\n42\t  `workspaces/<ws>/data_out/`), then home folder / Benny data / customware,\n43\t  Open Terminal Here, and Configure Home….\n44\t- **API** — `GET /api/home` on the Space server returns the resolved\n45\t  triple, each path's source, and any divergence warnings.\n46\t- **CLI** — `benny doctor` prints a `Home resolution` check with the same\n47\t  provenance; any legacy key or out-of-tree override shows as WARN.\n48\t- **Electron/IPC** — `ipcRenderer.invoke(\"space-desktop:get-home-directory\")`\n49\t  returns `{ homeDir, home }` where `home` is the full resolved report.\n50\t\n51\t## Configuring\n52\t\n53\t1. Right-click the tray icon → **Home** submenu → **\"Configure Home…\"** →\n54\t   pick (or create) a folder. `benny/` and `customware/` will live under it.\n55\t2. Restart Prime-Silo for the runtime to adopt the new location (the tray\n56\t   shows a `Runtime using: … (restart to apply new home)` line until then).\n57\t\n58\tThe setting persists in:\n59\t\n60\t- **Windows:** `%APPDATA%\\Prime-Silo\\prime-silo-config.json`\n61\t- **macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n62\t- **Linux:** `~/.config/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n63\t\n64\tFormat: `{ \"homeDir\": \"/path/to/home\" }`.\n65\t\n66\t## Legacy installs\n67\t\n68\tOlder versions used three independent locations. All of them keep working —\n69\tnothing is moved automatically — but each is flagged so you can adopt the\n70\tunified layout when ready:\n71\t\n72\t| Legacy mechanism                                                            | Behavior now                                                                                                |\n73\t| --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n74\t| `bennyHome` key in `prime-silo-config.json` (old \"Configure Benny Home…\")   | Honored (`legacy-config`); tray offers **\"Clear legacy Benny Home override\"** as the explicit adoption step |\n75\t| `<userData>/benny-home` and `<userData>/customware` (old per-user defaults) | Auto-detected when they exist (`legacy-default`) so existing data stays visible                             |\n76\t| `BENNY_HOME` env var pointing elsewhere                                     | Honored (`env-override`) with a divergence warning in doctor//api/home                                      |\n77\t\n78\tTo adopt the unified home: configure a home via the tray (or set\n79\t`PRIME_SILO_HOME`), move the contents of your old benny-home into\n80\t`<home>/benny/` and old customware into `<home>/customware/`, then clear\n81\tthe legacy override. `benny doctor` confirms when everything reports\n82\t`derived`.\n83\t\n84\t## For agents & scripts\n85\t\n86\t- Query `GET /api/home` instead of reading env vars.\n87\t- Python code must call `benny.portable.home.resolve_benny_home()` rather\n88\t  than `os.environ.get(\"BENNY_HOME\", <fallback>)` — cwd-relative fallbacks\n89\t  are how run debris used to end up committed to the repo.\n90\t- Node code (desktop/CLI/server) requires\n91\t  `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js`.\n92\t\n93\t## Troubleshooting\n94\t\n95\t- **\"Runtime using: … (restart to apply new home)\"** in the tray — you\n96\t  reconfigured the home while the bundled runtime was running. Quit and\n97\t  reopen Prime-Silo.\n98\t- **Doctor WARNs about a legacy key or env override** — expected until you\n99\t  adopt the unified layout (see \"Legacy installs\"); the WARN is the\n100\t  tripwire, not an error.\n101\t- **Home folder won't open** — the directory no longer exists; reconfigure\n102\t  via the tray.\n103\t"}]},"uuid":"291a76ec-1ed2-4763-a4f9-702d82846726","timestamp":"2026-07-23T11:47:25.844Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\HOME-DIRECTORY.md","content":"# Prime-Silo Home — the single declared home\n\nPrime-Silo keeps all of its workspace data under **one declared home\ndirectory**, with everything else derived from it:\n\n```\n<home>/                       ← the declared Prime-Silo home\n├── customware/               ← Space server data (L1/L2 modules)   → CUSTOMWARE_PATH\n└── benny/                    ← portable Benny runtime              → $BENNY_HOME\n    ├── bin/  config/  data/  workspaces/  models/  logs/  state/  …\n```\n\nOne resolver decides where the home is, and every process — the desktop\nshell, the tray, the Space server, `node space serve/supervise`, and the\nPython runtime — asks the same resolver:\n\n- Node: `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js` (`resolveHome()`)\n- Python: `benny.portable.home.resolve_home()` / `resolve_benny_home()`\n\n## Resolution precedence (highest wins)\n\n| #   | Source                                                                 | Provenance tag |\n| --- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| 1   | `PRIME_SILO_HOME` environment variable                                 | `env`          |\n| 2   | `homeDir` in `prime-silo-config.json` (set via tray \"Configure Home…\") | `config`       |\n| 3   | Per-user default: `<appData>/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-home`               | `default`      |\n\nDerived paths can still be overridden individually — an explicit\n`BENNY_HOME` or `CUSTOMWARE_PATH` env var always wins for its own path —\nbut the override is _reported_, not silent: it carries an `env-override`\nsource tag and a divergence warning when it points outside the declared\nhome.\n\n**There is no repo-relative fallback.** Nothing writes into a git checkout\nwhen the home is unconfigured; the per-user default is used instead.\n\n## Checking where your home is (and why)\n\n- **Tray** — right-click the Prime-Silo tray icon: one `Home: <name> (source)`\n  entry whose submenu holds everything home-related — **Open workspaces\n  (runs & outputs)** first (that's where generated deliverables land, e.g.\n  `workspaces/<ws>/data_out/`), then home folder / Benny data / customware,\n  Open Terminal Here, and Configure Home….\n- **API** — `GET /api/home` on the Space server returns the resolved\n  triple, each path's source, and any divergence warnings.\n- **CLI** — `benny doctor` prints a `Home resolution` check with the same\n  provenance; any legacy key or out-of-tree override shows as WARN.\n- **Electron/IPC** — `ipcRenderer.invoke(\"space-desktop:get-home-directory\")`\n  returns `{ homeDir, home }` where `home` is the full resolved report.\n\n## Configuring\n\n1. Right-click the tray icon → **Home** submenu → **\"Configure Home…\"** →\n   pick (or create) a folder. `benny/` and `customware/` will live under it.\n2. Restart Prime-Silo for the runtime to adopt the new location (the tray\n   shows a `Runtime using: … (restart to apply new home)` line until then).\n\nThe setting persists in:\n\n- **Windows:** `%APPDATA%\\Prime-Silo\\prime-silo-config.json`\n- **macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n- **Linux:** `~/.config/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n\nFormat: `{ \"homeDir\": \"/path/to/home\" }`.\n\n## Legacy installs\n\nOlder versions used three independent locations. All of them keep working —\nnothing is moved automatically — but each is flagged so you can adopt the\nunified layout when ready:\n\n| Legacy mechanism                                                            | Behavior now                                                                                                |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bennyHome` key in `prime-silo-config.json` (old \"Configure Benny Home…\")   | Honored (`legacy-config`); tray offers **\"Clear legacy Benny Home override\"** as the explicit adoption step |\n| `<userData>/benny-home` and `<userData>/customware` (old per-user defaults) | Auto-detected when they exist (`legacy-default`) so existing data stays visible                             |\n| `BENNY_HOME` env var pointing elsewhere                                     | Honored (`env-override`) with a divergence warning in doctor//api/home                                      |\n\nTo adopt the unified home: configure a home via the tray (or set\n`PRIME_SILO_HOME`), move the contents of your old benny-home into\n`<home>/benny/` and old customware into `<home>/customware/`, then clear\nthe legacy override. `benny doctor` confirms when everything reports\n`derived`.\n\n## For agents & scripts\n\n- Query `GET /api/home` instead of reading env vars.\n- Python code must call `benny.portable.home.resolve_benny_home()` rather\n  than `os.environ.get(\"BENNY_HOME\", <fallback>)` — cwd-relative fallbacks\n  are how run debris used to end up committed to the repo.\n- Node code (desktop/CLI/server) requires\n  `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js`.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n- **\"Runtime using: … (restart to apply new home)\"** in the tray — you\n  reconfigured the home while the bundled runtime was running. Quit and\n  reopen Prime-Silo.\n- **Doctor WARNs about a legacy key or env override** — expected until you\n  adopt the unified layout (see \"Legacy installs\"); the WARN is the\n  tripwire, not an error.\n- **Home folder won't open** — the directory no longer exists; reconfigure\n  via the tray.\n","numLines":103,"startLine":1,"totalLines":103}},"sourceTo