itted (Stream A)\n    Given LONGVIEW cards + ADRs + session synthesis in the corpus\n    When build_dataset.mjs runs\n    Then it emits JSONL (instruction -> house-style response) pairs that validate against the schema\n\n  Scenario: agent trajectories are emitted (Stream B)\n    Given Benny / offload / Claude tool-use traces\n    When build_dataset.mjs runs\n    Then it emits (state + goal -> next tool call) sequences that validate against the schema\n\n  Scenario: the leak gate blocks personal context\n    Given a row derived from job-application or CV session content\n    When the leak gate scans the emitted rows\n    Then that row is excluded and the gate reports zero personal-context leaks in the output\n\n  Scenario: a held-out eval set is reserved before training\n    Given the full emitted set\n    When the split runs\n    Then a disjoint held-out set is written and never appears in the train split\n```\n\n## Out of scope\nRunning the fine-tune (T3), DPO preference pairs (T5), any model download/serving. Data only.\n\n## Handoff\nVerifier re-runs `node scripts/gates/t2.mjs` from a clean checkout. `docs/train/T2-dataset-card.md`\nrecords row counts per stream, the split ratio, source provenance, and the leak-gate summary.\n","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0bd4d619-c7b8-4f02-8079-d42947e2be6c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"61a9f7a2-1353-4f19-addd-895289cb8f19","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
