ge → GGUF; gate green only if tuned ≥ base on the rubric.\n35\t\n36\t## Acceptance (BDD)\n37\t```gherkin\n38\tFeature: the tuned model is measurably better than its base, honestly\n39\t  Scenario: the eval instrument exists and scores the base first\n40\t    Given the held-out eval set from T2 and a defined rubric\n41\t    When the eval harness runs against the untuned base\n42\t    Then a baseline score is recorded per task category\n43\t\n44\t  Scenario: QLoRA training completes on the proven trainer\n45\t    Given the T2 train split and the T0-proven ROCm device\n46\t    When the QLoRA run executes\n47\t    Then loss is logged, the run completes, and a LoRA adapter is saved\n48\t\n49\t  Scenario: the tuned model beats base on the held-out set\n50\t    Given base and tuned scored by the same rubric with RAG disabled\n51\t    When the eval report is generated\n52\t    Then the tuned model's aggregate score is >= base and the delta is recorded (no unmeasured claims)\n53\t\n54\t  Scenario: the adapter merges to a loadable GGUF\n55\t    Given the trained adapter\n56\t    When it is merged and exported to GGUF\n57\t    Then the GGUF loads in the target runtime without error\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t## Out of scope\n61\tServing / router wiring (T4), DPO (T5). If tuned does NOT beat base, that is an honest result — log\n62\tit, do not tune the rubric to pass.\n63\t\n64\t## Handoff\n65\tVerifier re-runs `scripts/gates/t3.py`. `docs/train/T3-eval-report.md` is the KR1.5 evidence: base vs\n66\ttuned table per category, the delta, base-model choice, hyperparameters, and dataset provenance.\n67\t"}]},"uuid":"3d592a9c-696f-4802-9b8a-9cab06b88ee8","timestamp":"2026-07-23T14:46:43.488Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\delivery\\tasks\\T3.md","content":"---\nid: T3\nepic: EP-T\nmilestone: M3\nokr: O1.KR1.5\ndeps: [T0, T2]\nauthority: agent-ok\ntools: [rocm, unsloth, python]\nallowlist: [scripts/train/qlora/, scripts/train/eval/, scripts/gates/t3.py, docs/train/T3-eval-report.md]\nsandbox: in-place          # runs on the T480 GPU\nverify: python scripts/gates/t3.py\nbudget: 400\n---\n\n# T3 — First QLoRA run + honest base-vs-tuned eval\n\n## Goal\nFine-tune the base on Stream A + B (from T2) and prove — with a number, not a claim — that the tuned\nmodel beats its base on a held-out method/agent eval. RAG is held *separate* so we measure the\nfine-tune's own contribution, not retrieval. Merge the adapter to GGUF for serving (T4).\n\n## Context pointers (never inline content)\n- Inputs: T2 dataset (train + held-out); T0-proven trainer (device string, working ROCm path)\n- Base: Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct (or Qwen3-8B — pick per T0 smoke + eval fit; record the choice)\n- Config: QLoRA rank 16, lr 2e-4, packed ~16k ctx (from design plan \"Phase 2\")\n- Eval instrument = KR1.5's instrument: held-out method-style tasks + tool-call correctness, scored\n  base vs tuned. Define the rubric BEFORE training (no moving goalposts)\n- Design plan: `~/.claude/plans/mellow-tinkering-swan.md` — \"Phase 2\"\n\n## TDD plan\n1. `scripts/gates/t3.py` red: asserts an eval report exists comparing base vs tuned on the held-out\n   set with a recorded delta, and a merged GGUF loads. Fails with reason `no_eval` / `gguf_load_fail`.\n2. Eval harness first (runs base, produces baseline numbers) — proves the instrument before the run.\n3. QLoRA run; re-run eval on tuned; merge → GGUF; gate green only if tuned ≥ base on the rubric.\n\n## Acceptance (BDD)\n```gherkin\nFeature: the tuned model is measurably better than its base, honestly\n  Scenario: the eval instrument exists and scores the base first\n    Given the held-out eval set from T2 and a defined rubric\n    When the eval harness runs against the untuned base\n    Then a baseline score is recorded per task category\n\n  Scenario: QLoRA training completes on the proven trainer\n    Given the T2 train split and the T0-proven ROCm device\n    When the QLoRA run executes\n    Then loss is logged, the run completes, and a LoRA adapter is saved\n\n  Scenario: the tuned model beats base on the held-out set\n    Given base and tuned scored by the same rubric with RAG disabled\n    When the eval report is generated\n    Then the tuned model's aggregate score is >= base and the delta is recorded (no unmeasured claims)\n\n  Scenario: the adapter merges to a loadable GGUF\n    Given the trained adapter\n    When it is merged and exported to GGUF\n    Then the GGUF loads in the target runtime without error\n```\n\n## Out of scope\nServing / router wiring (T4), DPO (T5). If tuned does NOT beat base, that is an honest result — log\nit, do not tune the rubric to pass.\n\n## Handoff\nVerifier re-runs `scripts/gates/t3.py`. `docs/train/T3-eval-report.md` is the KR1.5 evidence: base vs\ntuned table per category, the delta, base-model choice, hyperparameters, and dataset provenance.\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6fac16d0-38b7-412a-89e9-221715f20570","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"61a9f7a2-1353-4f19-addd-895289cb8f19","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"ancient-squishing-orbit"}
