{"parentUuid":"65a2d58b-8637-483e-b2b9-dc68364fe401","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdKAwPi3YGATZ6DebrXTL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm mapping out the T3 gate requirements—it needs a red-first validation that checks for an eval report comparing base and tuned models on a held-out set with recorded performance deltas, plus verification that a merged GGUF file loads successfully, with specific reason codes for failures. I also need to set up an eval harness in the training scripts that runs evaluations on both base and production models.\n\nThe full pipeline is: run eval on the base model to establish baseline numbers, execute a QLoRA training run on Stream A+B data and save the adapter, re-evaluate the tuned model, merge it into GGUF format, and only mark the gate green if tuned performance meets or exceeds baseline. I'll need to document this in a T3 eval report and define the rubric before training starts, using either Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct or Qwen3-8B as the base.\n\nThis is a real training job on actual hardware with real time constraints—7B QLoRA at 16k context on 16GB VRAM with single parallelism is going to be intensive. I need to author all the gate logic, eval harness, and training scripts first, then actually kick off the run on the eGPU.\n\nT3 is marked agent-ok and runs on the T480 GPU, so I can proceed. For Phase 1, I'll define the eval rubric as a data structure using the held-out splits from T2 (stream_a.eval.jsonl and stream_b.eval.jsonl). For Stream A method/voice tasks, I'll score using held-out perplexity on the reference completion—it's deterministic and doesn't require a judge or network. For Stream B tool-call correctness, I'll use exact or structural matching of the predicted tool invocation.\n\nThe primary metric will be held-out negative log-likelihood for both streams, with tool-name exact-match generation as a secondary check—this keeps everything robust and deterministic within the 16GB constraint.\n\nThe gate script will verify that the tuned model achieves lower NLL than the base on the held-out set, then check that the eval report and merged GGUF file both exist and load correctly.\n\nThe eval harness computes cross-entropy loss per stream and tool-name accuracy, while the QLoRA training script handles the actual fine-tuning with Unsloth on the Qwen base model using rank-16 adapters and a learning rate of 2e-4.\n\nI need to be careful about context length — 16k is risky on a 7B model with 4-bit quantization on 16GB VRAM, so I might need to drop it to 4k or 8k and document that choice. After training on the combined stream splits, I'll merge the adapter back to GGUF format using either Unsloth's built-in export or llama.cpp's conversion tools.\n\nThe execution plan is to write everything first, run baseline eval to validate the pipeline, then start the QLoRA training in the background while I handle other tasks — but I need to verify the eGPU is actually connected and ready.\n\nBefore diving into heavy authoring, let me check if the GPU is available right now and locate the trainer venv, then mark the chapter and claim the task on the board.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2580,"cache_read_input_tokens":73159,"output_tokens":2757,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2580,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2757,"cache_read_input_tokens":73159,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2580,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2580},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdKAwKq8pbSszycNSdfqR","type":"assistant","uuid":"44cb7607-0ea6-4312-b2c0-bc631d18ae43","t