{"parentUuid":"aa7f4afb-5029-426c-9de4-a25e32f08668","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdKZLfDQBwLi88AFyQTLH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's my validation verdict while the rebuild runs — this is what the audit found and what I've changed:\n\n**Data validation findings (the training plan itself was sound; the data had three real defects):**\n\n1. **63% of Stream B rows had empty tool args** — an extraction bug, not source truth. Claude-format trace entities store the call as `{name, input}` but the pipeline only read `parsed.args`, so all 245 Claude rows (58% of B) were flattened to `{\"name\":\"Bash\",\"args\":{}}`. The model's headline B improvement (−77% NLL) was partly earned by learning to predict *degenerate* targets. **Fixed**: `args ?? input`, and unparseable content is now excluded rather than emitted empty.\n2. **Degenerate goals** — those same rows fell back to `goal: \"invoke Bash\"`. Claude's `input.description` (\"Verify push landed\") is a natural goal and is now used; key casing across agents handled.\n3. **Stream A template lock** — 55/56 rows shared one identical instruction phrase, teaching template-matching rather than method. Now 4 phrasings picked deterministically per card (FNV-1a over card id, so rebuilds and the train/eval split stay stable).\n\n**Corpus utilization:** T2 used only 6,000 of 80,555 memo-ray entities (7%) → 424 B train rows with 235 duplicate targets. The rebuild uses 40,000 entities / up to 2,500 rows — more sessions, more tool diversity, and duplicates collapse naturally once real args differentiate targets.\n\n**Training plan changes:** Stream A oversampled ×4 (else ~60 voice rows drown under ~2,500 trajectories), epochs 3→2 (more unique data, less repetition risk). Kept: r16/lr2e-4/cosine, response-only masking, frozen NLL rubric. One deliberate non-change: I'm **not** adding knowledge-graph fact-recall rows — the plan's design decision is fine-tune = method/tool-use, facts stay in RAG; cramming KG facts into weights would fight that.\n\n**Honesty note:** the rebuilt eval split is bigger/different, so I'll re-run the **base** eval on the identical new split before comparing — the rubric's metric and pass rule are unchanged, but base-vs-tuned must be computed on the same instrument. All of this is logged as an owner-directed data refresh (streams.mjs is T2-allowlist territory; your directive covers the amendment, and the T2 gate re-validates leak/schema/split).\n\nThe 40k-entity rebuild is reading from disk now; when it finishes I'll re-audit, then kick off baseline eval → training (~2h) → tuned eval → GGUF merge on D:."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":90,"cache_read_input_tokens":198424,"output_tokens":914,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":90,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":914,"cache_read_input_tokens":198424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":90,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":90},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdKZLKidpNm3xfBSuUWRK","type":"assistant","uuid":"6ca131ff-3449-4c90-8b67-5c65ca458bd2","timestamp":"2026-07-23T19:41:31.264Z","effort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"61a9f7a2-1353-4f19-addd-895289cb8f19","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"ancient-squishing-orbit"}
