{"parentUuid":"0e798bb4-e801-4dff-a4c6-50b455984a8d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdNF54gFu4puX2RuReZj4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AqvkXRf4a8CKDMdqikvWv1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\verify-gpu-job-liveness.md","content":"---\nname: verify-gpu-job-liveness\ndescription: A tqdm/log line is NOT proof a GPU job is alive — verify liveness by CPU-time/artifacts (owner caught a false positive)\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\n**Never report a long GPU job as \"progressing\" from its log alone.** On 2026-07-25 a DPO run\nwedged at step 8/38 (~00:45) and sat frozen for ~6 hours; I read the stale `tqdm` progress\nline and told the owner \"~10 more minutes, training is progressing.\" It was a false positive\nthe owner caught with \"are you sure it's not a false positive.\"\n\n**Why:** `tqdm` writes with `\\r` and, when stderr is redirected to a file, flushes rarely — a\nfrozen log looks identical to a slow one. And the RDNA4 eGPU-over-Thunderbolt **wedges**\ntransiently (a known failure mode for this trainer): the process stays alive but blocked in a\nGPU driver wait, working set collapses to ~1–12 MB (a real 7B training proc holds GBs), and no\nnew steps or checkpoints appear.\n\n**How to apply — prove liveness, don't infer it:**\n- Compare the log's **mtime to now** (`stat -c %y`). Hours stale on a job that should take\n  minutes = wedged, not slow.\n- Confirm the process is **doing work**: take two CPU-time snapshots ~90s apart\n  (`Get-CimInstance Win32_Process ... UserModeTime+KernelModeTime`); a live compute job burns\n  CPU seconds, a wedged one does not. Working-set ~MB = blocked in a syscall.\n- Check for **advancing artifacts** (trainer/checkpoint-*, result JSON, adapter files).\n- To recover: kill the process tree (`Stop-Process -Id <pid> -Force` in PowerShell; use\n  `$procId` not `$id` — `$id:` is a parse error), verify the eGPU recovered with a device\n  matmul, then relaunch (cap `max_length` lower to reduce the memory pressure that can wedge\n  gfx1200). Background-poll CPU-time to confirm the relaunch is genuinely stepping.\n\nSee [[windows-rocm-training-gotchas]], [[t480-trainer-stack]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":588765,"output_tokens":1761,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1761,"cache_read_input_tokens":588765,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdNF4zR2WjJf2E3SC4NjJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"43222912-d209-4c73-bdbc-56a0039883b9","timestamp":"2026-07-25T05:43:49.012Z","effort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"61a9f7a2-1353-4f19-addd-895289cb8f19","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"ancient-squishing-orbit"}
